--- text
Your data request has been received

We received your request about the personal data that
[COMPANY_NAME] holds about you. The request type is
[REQUEST_TYPE], and its reference is [REQUEST_REFERENCE]. Quote
that reference in any message you send us about this request.

Request details

Reference: [REQUEST_REFERENCE]
Request type: [REQUEST_TYPE]
Received: [EVENT_TIME]
Response due by: [RESPONSE_DUE_DATE]

What happens next

We first check that the request came from the person the data is
about. If we can match it to the account registered to
[EMAIL_ADDRESS], no further step is needed.

If we cannot, we will write to [EMAIL_ADDRESS] from
[SUPPORT_EMAIL] and ask you for something that confirms who you
are. We will never ask you for your password.

We will then work through the request and write to you with our
response on or before [RESPONSE_DUE_DATE].

The response date can be extended in specific circumstances, for
example when a request is complex or when you have made several
requests at once. If that happens here, we will tell you before
[RESPONSE_DUE_DATE], and give you the new date and the reason for
it.

Questions about this request go to [SUPPORT_EMAIL], or you can
reply to this email. Quote [REQUEST_REFERENCE] so we can find the
request.

[SIGNOFF_NAME], [COMPANY_NAME]
